  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan: Ethical Lifestyle Initiative for the Economic Reintegration of Returnees and Internally displaced people</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 4 year project aims to develop two broad value chains in the lifestyle market as tools to create sustainable employment and livelihoods for documented and undocumented returnees, internally displaced people, potential migrants, farmers and artisans. The Ethical Fashion Initiative (EFI) will focus on the following markets: Fashion and interiors; Fine foods. EFI will contribute to the implementation of the Citizens Charter National Priority Program (CCNPP), the Return and Reintegration Response and the overarching National Peace and Development Framework, Afghanistans Agribusiness Charter, the National Export Strategy (NES) and other initiatives linked to fashion, agriculture and displacement in Afghanistan. The project will work with works with twelve (12) social enterprises as implementing partners targeting 2,000 direct beneficiaries and up to 6,000 indirect beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
